    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106-a9">

                <pb facs="0256" n="200" xml:id="pg200"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 18,
                        1875</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Having been shown a proposed code of
                    signals for fog to be used by steam and sailing vessels, when under way and at
                    anchor, I am of opinion that the more simple the better, and less likely to lead
                    to mistakes; and would suggest that one long blast, say blown at least every
                    three minutes, one short blast to mean, “I am porting;” two, “I am
                    starboarding,” and three, “for danger,” “I am stopped,” or “reversing full
                    speed.”</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBERT E. BENCE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chief Officer Steamship
                            Ardiatic</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ismay, Imrie</hi> &amp; Co.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
